# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Documentation

## Start here

For a new idea, start with [Product Brief](product/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md) and [Readiness Assessment](operations/READINESS.md). Record known facts, open assumptions and one next action.

| Requested depth | Work now | Defer unless needed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Workspace-only | Brief facts, open questions, next action | Research execution, full design system, architecture and feature packets |
| Design-ready | Problem evidence, relevant rules, chosen journey, states and validation | Detailed implementation planning |
| Code-ready | Design scope plus contracts, concrete acceptance and first packet | Unrelated features and release operations |
| Implementation | Authorized scoped work and affected status | Scope not requested |

The initializer includes the full template kit. File presence does not make every section mandatory or establish readiness. Reuse equivalent existing documents.

For existing or implemented features, open [Feature Status](engineering/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md) to see what works, what remains, and the next action for each feature. Follow its links for detailed decisions and evidence.

## Source-of-truth order

1. `AGENTS.md` - repository safety and agent rules.
2. `product/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md` - users, problem, outcomes, scope.
3. `design/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` and `design/FLOW_AND_SCREEN_SPEC.md` - experience and state acceptance.
4. `engineering/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `engineering/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - technical decisions and delivery.
5. Active feature packet - current scoped handoff.
6. `engineering/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md` - one concise feature overview with verified facts and links to detail.
7. `operations/HANDOFF.md` - current operational context.

Read [Readiness Assessment](operations/READINESS.md) for evidence supporting the current stage and unresolved gates.

## Workflow

```text
discovery
→ design-ready
→ code-ready
→ in-progress
→ verification
→ accepted
→ released
```

